{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794258781,"nonce":"gsurW46UlYQm3m1YcrHy6PAABvk=","title":"Stateful registries are only ever added to, and SharedState refers to itself through Arc","message":"From the allocation audit (code read; growth not observed in a running app).\n\nblinc_layout stateful.rs: `STATEFUL_DEPS` is only inserted into; `clear_stateful_deps` and `clear_stateful_animations` have no callers. Each refresh closure holds `Arc\u003cSharedState\u003e`, and dead statefuls keep queuing refreshes. `PERSISTED_ANIMATED_VALUES` / `TIMELINES` / `KEYFRAME_TRACKS` are never removed from; the `Arc` is held, so the `AnimatedValue` never drops and its scheduler slot stays.\n\n`SharedState` also refers to itself: `state_callback` captures `shared_state_clone` and `refresh_callback` captures `shared_for_refresh`. There is no `Weak` in the file, so pruning the maps frees nothing until the cycle is broken.","files":null}]}